4. Deployment Readiness (Major Feature)

Deployment readiness is one of the most valuable capabilities of the portal.

The system validates deployments directly from Kubernetes.

It verifies:

* Test-3
* Test-4
* Stage West
* Production East
* Production West

For every component it validates:

* Deployment status
* Environment status
* Latest deployed Git SHA
* Latest release branch Git SHA
* Branch alignment
* Deployment freshness

If an environment is behind the release branch, the portal clearly identifies the gap.

Example:

Deployment is behind latest release by 2 commits.

This immediately informs Release Managers that redeployment is required before promotion.

This capability does not currently exist in the existing release process and significantly reduces deployment-related risks.

